      "full_page": "God bless you this blessed day of the Lord, - you and yours. Many thanks for your kind favor of several weeks back. I started a number of times to acknowledge same. I hope my tardiness may not scandalize. Not only this favor, however, do I want to thank you, but more I want to assure you of our appreciation of your generous activity these several years in the really privileged, though not less arduous work of the holy foreign missions. I am sure that the Good God will bless - has blessed - you in many ways for your practical interest in this outstanding phase of really Catholic action. Besides this, I want to congratulate you on your having been so guided as to be able to write of a business associate as you do of the young man with whom you condole on the death of his amiable mother. It is always a relief to know of such a person. The very fact of his having been a \"bible student\" ought to spell something in his favor. This, even though, for want of proper guidance, many a \"bible student\" has anchored in dangerous waters. But these days when atheism, the very climax of intellectual stupidity, of moral insanity, of diabolically devilish perversity; it is a hopeful indication to see anyone of good will taking more than ordinary interest in the divine messages from Heaven as are those conveyed to humanity through the inspired writings, the divinely guided compilation and the appreciative, prayerful study of the Holy Bible. This all the more now, that in the family of governments one of even the \"big powers\" is not only permitted to show its shamelessly criminal face, but brazenly to insist on dictating hell's own principles of peace. Indeed an unmistakable indication whither our godless system of public-education is, not only tending but tumbling; unless by an effective S.O.S. call of true religion. Pardon my digression. I would have enrolled your friend-associate as also his deceased mother, but I did find their names. I have no doubt but that they would both profit thereby. So if you just send me their names I shall be glad to do that for you and for them. Wishing you and yours God's blessing again for a happy day of national Thanksgiving; and especially in case you do not in the mean time hear from me again, the grace of a blessed and happy Christmas celebration with all success for the coming New Year and thereafter. Sincerely Yours in Christ.",
      "per_polygon": "God bless you this blessed day of the Lord, - you and yours. Many thanks for your kind favor of several weeks back. I started a number of times to acknowledge same. I hope my tardiness may not scandalize. Not only this favor, however, do I want to thank you, but more I want to assure you of our appreciation of your generous activity these several years in the really privileged, though not less arduous work of the holy foreign missions. I am sure that the Good God will bless - has blessed - you in many ways for your practical interest in this outstanding phase of really Catholic action. Besides this, I want to congratulate you on your having been so guided as to be able to write of a business associate as you do of the young man with whom you condole on the death of his amiable mother. It is always a relief to know of such a person. The very fact of his having been a \"bible student\" ought to spell something in his favor. This, even though, for want of proper guidance, many a \"bible student\" has anchored in dangerous waters. But these days when atheism, the very climax of intellectual stupidity, of moral insanity, of diabolically devilish perversity; it is a hopeful indication to see anyone of good will taking more than ordinary interest in the divine messages from Heaven as are those conveyed to humanity through the inspired writings, the divinely guided compilation and the appreciative, prayerful study of the Holy Bible. This all the more now, that in the family of governments one of even the \"big powers\" is not only permitted to show its shamelessly criminal face, but brazenly to insist on dictating hell's own principles of peace. Indeed an unmistakable indication whither our godless system of public-education is, not only tending but tumbling; unless by an effective S.O.S. call of true religion. Pardon my digression. I would have enrolled your friend-associate as also his deceased mother, but I did find their names. I have no doubt but that they would both profit thereby. So if you just send me their names I shall be glad to do that for you and for them. Wishing you and yours God's blessing again for a happy day of national Thanksgiving; and especially in case you do not in the mean time hear from me again, the grace of a blessed and happy Christmas celebration with all success for the coming New Year and thereafter. Sincerely Yours in Christ.",
